WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.400
TARGET MXene · METAL-LIKE CONDUCTIVITY · WEAKNESS: OXYGEN

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.400
OPERATION OXIDATION · A NANOSCALE HEIST

3
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.900
WHAT IS MXene? A thin material that conducts like a metal

4
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.900
Exposed to oxygen in air, MXene oxidizes

5
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.400
THE PROBLEM: Rapid oxidation in air and at high temperature held back real-world use

6
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.900
Same break-in. Different ending? (BEFORE | THIS WORK)

7
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.800
BEFORE: No one to stop them | THIS WORK: MnO₂ NANOPARTICLE SECURITY

8
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.400
Illustration · not the real reaction speed

9
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
BEFORE: DEGRADED | THIS WORK: LESS OXIDATION

10
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.000
MnO₂ preferentially interacts with oxygen and greatly mitigates MXene oxidation (Shown by DFT and XPS)

11
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.000
Air and high temperature: BEFORE Oxidizes fast | THIS WORK Oxidation greatly reduced · MnO₂ preferentially interacts with oxygen (DFT, XPS)

12
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Real devices: BEFORE Hard to use | THIS WORK Fully 3D-printed device · 0D/1D/2D hybrid ink, no extra metal current collector

13
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.000
Printed device: 98.52% capacitance retention (after 10,000 charge–discharge cycles)

14
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.300
0D MnO₂ + 1D silver nanowires + 2D MXene hybrid ink

15
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.000
WHERE IT COULD GO: Printed energy storage for flexible electronics

16
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.000
10–50 °C · stable across a wide temperature range

17
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.000
Oxygen-scavenging MnO₂, oxidation-resistant MXene ink

18
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.600
Busted!
